{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 776930b7d28637cba8ed0f05047017f9a3266695 on planner/publisher-member-20261113, its one artifact `notes/2026-11-13-publisher-member.md`, for request 35cbcb29 under promise 885d9876 and review request 8e48f694. Draft 2 answers verdict cbc9626c, and its one commit since ffa498e2 changes only the parts that the verdict named.\n\nWhat I read, since ffa498e2:\n\n- Required change 1. Section 7 states that revoking a publisher has two parts: membership revokes the key, and the issuer of the Git credential revokes it at the host. It states what the old publisher can still do until the second part is done: move the branch, which the new publisher meets as \"Another writer moved the branch\". It names the issuer as the holder of the duty, for an operator and for a room's owner. The rows of sections 6 and 7 follow. Section 11 lists the decision on who runs a hosted publisher as Hugh's.\n- Required change 2. Section 4.2 names both guards on `through`: the `fact` guard and `equals { a: { field: \"through\", part: \"scope\" }, b: { scope: true } }`. It states why the first is not enough. Witness 9 covers a `through` of another scope under a definition of the same name, and the scope refuses it.\n- My three facts for P1: `repository` is not required, the note names the role table in `dap.application.json` and the `set-actions` act, and the field type of `through` lists each kind it can name.\n\nWhat I checked: main 57e893c0 is an ancestor, and the head changes one path. The artifact covers it at the head and is neither stale nor retired. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (4 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The conclusions of cbc9626c stand. My kernel reading stands too: slice P1 changes `examples/lending` alone and names no K item.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The record now states which part of a revocation it can enforce and which part the credential's issuer must do, and the cursor can name only an entry of its own scope.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing. Hugh ratifies the note and makes the two decisions of section 11.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cc22611313c4d32a437b28a7be336cc3b6de60c9","binding":"assigned","head":"776930b7d28637cba8ed0f05047017f9a3266695","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0bfd3a680076f459c304f480c1520558c9945e8f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:885d9876ee81ce9ccee711063914f38e3a4c04bc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7227d3107cc06607d5f805a0491c766bf1917d97","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}